# respawn.play — DEATH IS A SETBACK, NOT AN ENDING, AND THE CHARACTER SURVIVES IT.
#
# DESIGN §3a puts checkpoint respawn among the deliberate departures from Angband: the
# systems are faithful, the DEATH MODEL is friendlier. That is a design commitment, so
# it deserves a gate that fails if someone quietly restores permadeath — and the only
# place the whole rule exists is flow_move, which discovers `sim_over` and respawns.
#
# ⚠ THE SETUP USES POKES AND THE CLAIM DOES NOT. `findstair` and `hurt` arrange a death
# at depth 2; the respawn itself is left to a `move` row, so what is being tested is
# still the shipped movement path. A script that called sim_respawn directly would pass
# while the game was broken.
#
# ⚠ AND THE STRONGEST CLAIM IS "IT DID NOT CHANGE". The kit surviving death is exactly
# the class of bug that made flow_genesis a SHARED boot in the first place — a replica
# that missed a step looked fine until you inspected the pack. `remember` before, compare
# after; a literal there would only pin this week's starting kit.

genesis 1337 1
echo --- go down one level, so the checkpoint is somewhere we are NOT

findstair
move 0 0 1
expect depth == 2

remember died_at depth
remember kit inv
remember purse gold
remember pool hpmax
note savedepth

echo --- die (a poke: empty the pool; nothing has discovered it yet)
hurt 999
expect hp == 0
expect alive == 0

# ⚠ THE WORLD DOES NOT KNOW YET. Death is discovered by the movement path, not by the
# damage — this row is the difference between testing the rule and testing sim_damage.
expect depth == died_at

echo --- one movement tick: flow_move discovers the death and respawns
move 0 0 1

echo --- alive again, at the checkpoint, with the character intact
expect alive == 1
expect depth == savedepth
expect depth != died_at

# Restored to FULL, and to the same pool as before — a respawn that quietly rerolled
# the character would satisfy `hp > 0` and be a different person.
expect hp == hpmax
expect hpmax == pool

# The pack crosses death untouched. This is the row the whole script exists for.
expect inv == kit

echo --- and the price was paid in gold, left where we fell
# Half the purse is staked on a grave at the depth of the death: measured 30 -> 15 with
# 15 on the grave. Asserted as relations because the FRACTION is tuning, but the two
# facts that are not tuning are that something is staked and that it is left BEHIND.
expect gravegold > 0
expect gravedepth == died_at
expect gold < purse
expect gold > 0
